ind a pawn shield.\n- Activates the h1 rook by connecting it with the queen and other pieces.\n- Is often more valuable than slow development when the position allows.\n\nCastling is time-efficient and reduces vulnerability. Other moves like Nc3 or Bf4 are good, but none offer the same combination of safety and long-term strategic benefit as castling.\n\nReason: Kingside castling is safe here and maximizes king safety while improving piece coordination. It’s a high-priority move in the opening phase, and delaying it risks wasting tempo or walking into tactical dangers later.\n\nAnswer: K: e1-g1"}
